If a clinician conducts an acute-pain-treatment with an opioid for an opioid-naive-patient during a few-day-period then an opioid-dosage-increase usually can be unnecessary for the opioid-naive-patient.
If a clinician increases an opioid-dosage during an acute-pain-treatment for an opioid-naive-patient during a few-day-period then the clinician should closely monitor the opioid-naive-patient.
